<html lang="en">
<head>
    <title>Partitioned Model</title>
    <style>
        h3 { ${REGULAR_LARGE_FONT_STYLE} }
        body { ${REGULAR_FONT_STYLE} }
        code { ${MONOSPACE_FONT_STYLE} }
        h3 code { font-size: inherit; }
        p { margin-top: 0; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h3>Partitioned Model</h3>
    <p>
        When enabled, Oracle trains a separate sub-model for each unique combination
        of partition column values (<code>ODMS_PARTITION_COLUMNS</code>).
    </p>
    <p>
        Partitioned models allow a single model object to represent multiple
        sub-populations — useful when data behaviour varies across groups
        (e.g. per region, per product category).
    </p>
    <p>Select the partition columns in the list below.</p>
</body>
</html>
